summaries.auth:
Accounts are individual Supabase Auth users with one public.profiles row each. The role is global (app_role staff|manager|admin) and there is a single profiles.venue_id. There are no per-venue memberships. Manager rights come from venue_manager_grants and only take effect for the account's current venue (private.effective_manager_venue_id), so a person cannot manage pub A and contribute at pub B (AC14 cannot pass). Admin-only invitation (lib/server/accounts/invite.ts) uses email plus magic link or a 6-digit code, invite role is hard-coded to staff, and conversion to and from manager is audited (coverage_audit_events entity account_role). Deactivation sets profiles.active=false, applies an Auth ban and auto-revokes grants, and media is kept. RLS and storage policies re-read current profile state and have an adversarial suite (docs/security-tests.md, tests/security, tests/integration/isolation.test.ts). File-signature sniffing (sniffMedia in finalise.ts), log redaction (lib/server/log/redact.ts), private buckets, and a local backup/restore drill with byte comparison are in place. Biggest gaps:
- per-venue memberships;
- managers cannot invite or remove staff (AC40 missing);
- no MFA (config.toml [auth.mfa.totp] disabled) and no organisation session expiry;
- no explicit shared-device mode: sign-out always clears drafts;
- staff can permanently delete their own accepted media (delete_media_asset), which conflicts with the spec's admin-only deletion with a reason;
- managers cannot download originals; admins cannot upload;
- orphan cleanup uses a 24 h window that is not scheduled anywhere;
- hosted restore and storage-capacity alerting are untested or missing;
- last-admin protection is only implicit, because admins cannot be managed in the app at all.
